                                        "entry_id": "a6bcef91-ea72-302f-8434-d214710bd998",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A substance first obtained from guano; it is a nucleic base and pairs with cytosine in DNA and RNA (by means of three hydrogen bonds)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0407e6f4-1e79-4c18-abcc-0cc5627e3291",
                                                "sense_id": "ddeb0e90-1dd3-323a-b90e-6aff4a87ec8d",
                                                "text": "Then he found them, the substances that made up the four-letter alphabet in whose language all life is written — adenine and cytosine, guanine and thymine."
                                            }
